  "family": "Platanaceae",
  "memo": "&lt;em&gt;Platanus acerifolia ‘Columbia’ &lt;/em&gt;is a cultivar of London Plane Tree, which is a hybrid of &lt;em&gt;P. occidentalis&lt;/em&gt; and &lt;em&gt;P. orientalis. &lt;/em&gt;It was developed in 1984 for its resistance to anthranose and mildew. This fast-growing tree forms a slender trunk with a rounded, shade-providing canopy. Its bark is very attractive, peeling in patches of light brown, yellow, and orange. Palmately-lobed leaves also transition to rich yellow tones in autumn, adding a layer of seasonal interest. This graceful plant is perfect for urban planting, tolerant of smog, heat, wind, and poor soils.&nbsp;",
